 {"file": "tests/py/test_reeds.py", "test": "test_T104_spectrum_is_rich_and_not_darker_when_louder", "problem": "(a) Requires the centroid at velocity 1.0 to be at least that at 0.3 for one note; real accordion ff is brighter than pp in only 85 % of pitches (C-055), so a faithful instrument can fail at A4. (b) harmonic_count_above counts the maximum of any 35-cent window as a partial, so broadband noise within 60 dB of the peak counts as harmonics: a sine plus noise passes 'rich spectrum'.", "suggested_fix": "(a) Allow a small tolerance (c_hi >= 0.95 c_lo) or require it on a majority of three notes; (b) count a partial only if its peak stands at least 10 dB above the median level of the surrounding inter-harmonic band."},
